{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>When it hails.</b> The resh is vowelized with patach, for it is a pa'al form like עשן כולו (Exodus 19:18). And the meaning: though hail comes down on the forest, it comes down — but not on the place of the seed." "And the meaning of <b>the city shall be laid low</b> is that it shall dwell unwalled, in the valley."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:24.227768760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}